        <article class="card reveal">
          <h2>Google Calendar and Google API Data</h2>
          <p>Classic Academy can connect to Google Calendar for the optional demo and booking feature. When an authorized administrator connects Google Calendar, Classic Academy requests only the Calendar permissions needed to check free/busy availability and create, update, or remove booking events associated with the Classic Academy booking service.</p>
          <p>Google Calendar data is used only to provide and improve the user-facing booking functionality requested by the authorized administrator. We do not use Google user data for advertising, retargeting, credit decisions, data-broker services, or to train general-purpose artificial intelligence or machine-learning models.</p>
          <p>When OAuth is used, Classic Academy stores the Google refresh credential in encrypted form so the booking service can continue to access the authorized Calendar without requiring the administrator to sign in for every booking. Calendar event and availability information is processed only as needed to perform booking operations, maintain service integrity, troubleshoot failures, and comply with applicable legal obligations.</p>
          <p>We do not sell Google user data. We do not share Google user data with third parties except service providers that are necessary to operate or secure the Service, when required by law, or when the user has expressly authorized the disclosure.</p>
          <p>An authorized administrator can disconnect Google Calendar from Classic Academy, revoke Classic Academy access from their Google Account permissions, or contact Us to request deletion of stored Google authorization credentials and related integration records, subject to any legal retention requirement.</p>
          <p>Classic Academy's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
        </article>

